# INVWINSM.KEY - a key script of INVWIN, as INVWIN.KEY: the record
# commands on several items of the item list at level 3.  Install in
# (ALT-C I) installs items 1 to 3 in item 2: one dialog, item 1
# installed, item 2 refused as itself, a box saying where it stopped,
# item 3 left, the list fetched again.  Take out (ALT-C T) takes them
# out to Office the same way, item 2 refused as not installed; with
# item 1 not installed either its own refusal shows in the dialog,
# which stays.  Move (ALT-C M) on Office, item 1's location, moves the
# other two there; Move to B2 moves all three, the note counting them.
# A right click on a selected row keeps the selection, the pop-up's
# Move acting on all of it, as SHIFT-F10's does; on another row it
# selects that row alone.  Move with one row chosen asks as for one
# item.  DEL asks once, naming the count: No keeps both, Yes deletes
# both; DEL on the one left asks as for one item.  The end by Exit.
# TEST/GOLDEN/WIN/INVWINSM.SNP is its snapshot; TEST/selchk.py checks
# it.
T ADMIN
K TAB
T Retro1986
K ENTER SHIFT-DOWN SHIFT-DOWN
S THREE
K ALT-C I
S ASKIN
T 2
K ENTER
S INSTOP
K ENTER
S INSTDONE
K HOME SHIFT-DOWN SHIFT-DOWN ALT-C T
S ASKOUT
T OFF
K ENTER
S OUTSTOP
K ENTER
S OUTDONE
# item 1, the first row, refused in the dialog: nothing done
K HOME SHIFT-DOWN SHIFT-DOWN ALT-C T
T A1
K ENTER
S OUTREF
K ESC Y
S OUTREFBK
K HOME SHIFT-DOWN SHIFT-DOWN ALT-C M
S ASKMOVE
K ENTER
S KEPT
K HOME SHIFT-DOWN SHIFT-DOWN ALT-C M
T B2
K ENTER
S MOVED
# the pop-up on item 1, selected with item 2
K HOME SHIFT-DOWN
M 208.1 RDOWN ROW 0
S RKEEPDN
M 208.1 RUP ROW 0
S RKEEP
K M
S RMOVE
T A1
K ENTER
S RMOVED
K HOME SHIFT-DOWN
M 208.1 RDOWN ROW 2
M 208.1 RUP ROW 2
S RONE
K ESC HOME SHIFT-DOWN SHIFT-F10
S F10POP
K M
S F10MOVE
K ESC HOME ALT-C M
S ONEMOVE
K ESC HOME SHIFT-DOWN DEL
S DELASK
K N
S DELNO
K DEL Y
S DELYES
K DEL
S DELONE
K N ALT-F X
